{"id":"ebbcc9984c010c150f50fbfb0265940b7e502129","axis":"silent","repo":"nrwl/nx","sha":"ebbcc9984c010c150f50fbfb0265940b7e502129","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"astro-docs/src/content/docs/kb/create-config.mdoc","lines":["@@ -19,8 +19,8 @@ It takes an optional `Configuration` object as an argument, which allows for cus"," On Rspack 2, `createConfig` turns lazy compilation off for the browser build by default."," To turn it on, set `rspackConfigOverrides.lazyCompilation` to `true`."," The override doesn't affect the server build.","-With server-side rendering (SSR), pages from the SSR server's port (`PORT`, 4000 by default)","-can't load lazily compiled code, because only the dev server compiles it.","+Without `ssr.serveFromDevServer`, pages from the server-side rendering (SSR) server's port","+(`PORT`, 4000 by default) can't load lazily compiled code, because only the dev server compiles it."," Use the dev-server URL, or keep lazy compilation off when you need server-rendered pages."," "," ```ts","@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@ export default createConfig({","   options: {","     browser: './src/main.ts',","     server: './src/main.server.ts',","-    ssr: { entry: './src/server.ts' },","+    ssr: { entry: './src/server.ts', serveFromDevServer: true },","   },"," });"," ```","@@ -91,7 +91,7 @@ export default createConfig({","   options: {","     browser: './src/main.ts',","     server: './src/main.server.ts',","-    ssr: { entry: './src/server.ts' },","+    ssr: { entry: './src/server.ts', serveFromDevServer: true },","   },","   rspackConfigOverrides: {","     mode: 'development',","@@ -112,7 +112,7 @@ export default createConfig({","   options: {","     browser: './src/main.ts',","     server: './src/main.server.ts',","-    ssr: { entry: './src/server.ts' },","+    ssr: { entry: './src/server.ts', serveFromDevServer: true },","     fileReplacements: [","       {","         replace: './src/environments/environment.ts',","@@ -168,6 +168,7 @@ export interface AngularRspackPluginOptions extends PluginUnsupportedOptions {","         platform?: 'node' | 'neutral';","         // Deprecated. Use `platform` instead.","         experimentalPlatform?: 'node' | 'neutral';","+        serveFromDevServer?: boolean;","       };","   stylePreprocessorOptions?: StylePreprocessorOptions;","   styles?: ScriptOrStyleEntry[];","@@ -384,9 +385,28 @@ Controls generation of source maps for debugging. Can be boolean or detailed con"," "," ### ssr"," ","-`boolean | { entry: string; platform?: 'node' | 'neutral' }`","+`boolean | { entry: string; platform?: 'node' | 'neutral'; serveFromDevServer?: boolean }`"," Configuration for Server-Side Rendering. Can be boolean or object with specific SSR settings. The `experimentalPlatform` option is deprecated; use `platform` instead."," ","+`serveFromDevServer` sets where `rspack serve` renders pages:","+","+- `true`: the dev server renders pages at its own URL.","+  It loads the server bundle and calls the `reqHandler` that `entry` exports, when","+  `createNodeRequestHandler` from `@angular/ssr/node` or `createRequestHandler` from `@angular/ssr` created it.","+  Otherwise it renders pages without that handler and doesn't serve the routes that `entry` adds, such as API routes.","+  After each server build, it loads the bundle again, so the top-level code in `entry` runs again.","+  `isMainModule(import.meta.url)` returns `false` in the bundle, so the `app.listen` block of generated applications doesn't run.","+  Applications that the `@nx/angular` generators create set it.","+  The `@nx/angular:convert-to-rspack` generator sets it when `entry` creates its own `reqHandler`","+  export with one of those functions.","+  Each file that replaces `entry` in `fileReplacements` must create its own `reqHandler` export the same way.","+- Not set: `rspack serve` runs the server bundle as a separate server.","+  It listens on the port that `entry` sets, `PORT` or 4000 in generated applications.","+  The dev-server URL serves the client-rendered application.","+  This mode is deprecated, and `rspack serve` prints a warning for it.","+","+Nx 25 removes the option and always renders pages on the dev server.","+"," ### stylePreprocessorOptions"," "," `StylePreprocessorOptions`"],"additions":26,"deletions":6,"truncated":false},{"path":"astro-docs/src/content/docs/kb/getting-started.mdoc","lines":["@@ -132,6 +132,8 @@ npx nx serve myapp"," This command will serve your Angular Rspack application.  "," For Client-Side Rendering (CSR) applications, the default port is `4200`. You can visit the application by navigating to `http://localhost:4200` in your browser."," ","-For Server-Side Rendering (SSR) applications, the default port is `4000`. You can visit the application by navigating to `http://localhost:4000` in your browser.","+SSR applications use the same port when they set `ssr.serveFromDevServer`,","+as generated applications do.","+For SSR applications without it, see the [`ssr` option of `createConfig`](/docs/kb/create-config#ssr)."," "," HMR is enabled by default so you can make changes to your application and see the changes in real-time."],"additions":3,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"astro-docs/src/content/docs/technologies/angular/introduction.mdoc","lines":["@@ -131,7 +131,8 @@ A task that depends on a dev server target starts once the server task has start"," To make it wait until the server accepts connections, set `waitFor` to `ready` on its `dependsOn` entry."," It then waits for the target's `readyWhen` check, which depends on how the target runs the server:"," ","-- `angular.json` targets that use a dev server or SSR dev server builder get a check from `@nx/angular/plugin`.","+- `angular.json` targets that use a dev server or server-side rendering (SSR) dev server builder","+  get a check from `@nx/angular/plugin`.","   It runs when the task runs, reads the target from `angular.json`, and waits for the port.","   The port comes from the `--port` flag, then the target's `port` option, which a configuration can override, then 4200.","   For `@angular/build:dev-server` 22 or later, a set `PORT` environment variable replaces it, as it does in the builder.","@@ -139,7 +140,10 @@ It then waits for the target's `readyWhen` check, which depends on how the targe","   Nx then reports the `baseUrl` that the builder returns.","   Generated targets include the setting, and a migration adds it to existing ones."," - Rspack applications get `\"readyWhen\": { \"signal\": true }` from `@nx/rspack/plugin`, and `NgRspackPlugin` reports the dev server's address once it listens.","-  With SSR, the server in `server.ts` reports its own address instead, when it calls `emitReadySignal` from `@nx/js/ready-signal`, as generated SSR servers do.","+  With SSR and `ssr.serveFromDevServer`, the dev server renders pages at that address","+  and reports it once the server bundle has loaded.","+  Without the option, the server in `server.ts` reports its own address instead,","+  when it calls `emitReadySignal` from `@nx/js/ready-signal`, as generated SSR servers do."," - The `serve-static` target runs the `@nx/web:file-server` executor, which reports its address once it listens."," "," With the last three, the waiting task gets the reported address in the `NX_READY_URL` environment variable."],"additions":6,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"astro-docs/src/content/docs/technologies/build-tools/rspack/introduction.mdoc","lines":["@@ -108,10 +108,17 @@ Angular Rspack configs made with `createConfig` from `@nx/angular-rspack` load `"," In other configs, add `new NxReadySignalPlugin()` from `@nx/rspack/ready-signal` to `plugins` instead."," The report carries the port the server actually uses, so the check is right however the port was chosen."," ","-In an Angular server-side rendering (SSR) app, the dev server reports once it listens, without waiting for the build.","+In an Angular server-side rendering (SSR) app that sets `ssr.serveFromDevServer`,","+the dev server renders the pages at its own address.","+It reports that address once the server bundle has loaded.","+","+Without the option, the SSR server starts only after the build,","+on `PORT` or the port its server file sets, 4000 in generated apps.","+When the server file calls `emitReadySignal` from `@nx/js/ready-signal`, as generated ones do,","+the SSR server reports its own address once it listens.","+Otherwise, the dev server reports once it listens, without waiting for the build."," It holds requests until the build finishes.","-The SSR server starts only after the build, on `PORT` or the port its server file sets, 4000 in generated apps.","-A task that tests SSR on that port has to wait for it itself.","+A task that tests SSR on the SSR server's port then has to wait for it itself."," "," Without any of these plugins, the check reads the Rspack config when the task runs instead, in the task's environment and with its options."," That covers `.env` files and `--port` or `--host` flags."],"additions":10,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"e2e/angular/src/projects-ssr.test.ts","lines":["@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@"," import {","+  addReadyUrlCheck,","   checkFilesDoNotExist,","   checkFilesExist,","+  expectServedOn,","   killProcessAndPorts,","   readFile,","   readJson,","@@ -12,13 +14,14 @@ import {","   tmpProjPath,","   uniq,","   updateFile,","-  waitUntil,"," } from '@nx/e2e-utils';","-import { chromium, type Browser, type Page } from '@playwright/test';","+import {","+  chromium,","+  type Browser,","+  type Page,","+  type WebSocket,","+} from '@playwright/test';"," import { spawn, type ChildProcess } from 'node:child_process';","-import { mkdtempSync, readFileSync, rmSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';","-import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';","-import { join } from 'node:path';"," import {","   setupProjectsTest,","   resetProjectsTest,","@@ -88,13 +91,9 @@ describe('Angular Projects - SSR', () => {","   }, 500_000);"," ","   it('should support the application engin